	quest_links: [ ]
	quests: [
		{
			description: [
				"Compared to other equipment mods, Weapon Master provides &5long-term progression&r, giving players a strong sense of growth and achievement."
				""
				"In addition, Weapon Master offers a level of visual design and equipment customization that is difficult for other equipment mods to match. Any player who has used its weapons is likely to be left with a lasting impression of the items within the mod."
			]
			icon: "weaponmaster:workstation"
			id: "1C3CABF6FA4DBB44"
			rewards: [{
				count: 4
				id: "2319A4D71F76480F"
				item: {
					Count: 1b
					id: "lightmanscurrency:coin_iron"
					tag: { }
				}
				type: "item"
			}]
			shape: "rsquare"
			subtitle: "Why choosing Weapon Master"
			tasks: [{
				id: "3D01795BE150312C"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Intro : Weapon Master"
			x: 1.0d
			y: 3.25d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["1C3CABF6FA4DBB44"]
			description: [
				"To begin your Weapon Master journey, a simple Weapon Studio is not enough, you will need to craft a &5Weapon Kit&r to choose your weapon."
				""
				"By &eright-clicking&r the Weapon Kit, a selection interface containing four different weapons will appear. Based on your preference, you can choose a weapon to accompany you on your adventure. Of course, you can also craft four Weapon Kits and take one of each！"
			]
			id: "4B92B6F9C9EDC46E"
			rewards: [{
				id: "20A85C308C640405"
				item: {
					Count: 1b
					id: "lightmanscurrency:coin_gold"
					tag: { }
				}
				type: "item"
			}]
			subtitle: "A lifelong companion"
			tasks: [{
				id: "4408346A4E2B3C20"
				item: "weaponmaster:weaponkit"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "Choose Your Weapon！"
			x: 2.75d
			y: 3.25d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["4B92B6F9C9EDC46E"]
			description: [
				"After selecting your weapon, you will notice that its default durability is 0. To restore it, you need to use the Weapon Studio mentioned earlier to maintain your weapon."
				""
				"Right-click the Weapon Studio and place your chosen weapon into the slot in the GUI. Then select the button below to enter &2Repair Mode&r."
				""
				"In this mode, first apply &2Weapon Repair Paste&r over the entire weapon, then use a &2cloth (sandpaper?)&r to polish it. Once completed, the weapon will emit a &6glowing effect&r."
				""
				"After finishing one side, click the &2button on the right&r to flip it over and repeat the process. Once all steps are completed, the weapon’s durability will be fully restored."
				""
				"{image:kubejs:textures/task/weapon_master_1.png width:160 height:90 align:1}"
			]
			icon: "hexerei:cloth"
			id: "2C8054AE6C57197F"
			rewards: [{
				count: 3
				id: "361C99A0FA76F713"
				item: {
					Count: 1b
					id: "lightmanscurrency:coin_iron"
					tag: { }
				}
				type: "item"
			}]
			subtitle: "First Weapon Maintenance"
			tasks: [{
				id: "4D956F29048CE985"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Polish Your Weapon"
			x: 1.0d
			y: 1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["2C8054AE6C57197F"]
			description: [
				"After repairing your weapon, you can use the right-side buttons in the Weapon Studio to view four weapon attributes: &2damage, attack speed, durability, and looting&r."
				""
				"By &eselecting different attribute bars on the right with your mouse&r, any experience gained during use will be allocated to that specific attribute."
				""
				"For example, if you want to increase your weapon’s damage, you should select the damage attribute line."
				""
				"{image:kubejs:textures/task/weapon_master_2.png width:160 height:90 align:1}"
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"When a weapon’s experience bar is fully filled, its corresponding attribute level will increase. At this point, placing the weapon back into the Weapon Studio will open an upgrade interface."
				"In this interface, you can select &2three weapon visual&r at the top, and &2one ability&r at the bottom."
				""
				"Weapon visuals and abilities will continue to appear during each upgrade until you have unlocked all available visuals and abilities."
				""
				"Once unlocked, weapon visuals can be configured using the top button, while abilities can be configured using the left-side button."
				""
				"{image:kubejs:textures/task/weapon_master_3.png width:160 height:90 align:1}"
			]
			icon: "modulargolems:quartz"
			id: "09F28AC07C32FAB3"
			rewards: [{
				count: 3
				id: "01F5CA3B2A4C633C"
				item: {
					Count: 1b
					id: "lightmanscurrency:coin_iron"
					tag: { }
				}
				type: "item"
			}]
			subtitle: "leveling, visuals and abilities"
			tasks: [{
				id: "229906B9C02325A9"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Weapon Leveling"
			x: -0.75d
			y: 3.25d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["09F28AC07C32FAB3"]
			description: [
				"At this point, nearly all gameplay content of Weapon Master has been introduced. As a lightweight weapon-focused mod, Weapon Master undoubtedly achieves a &5compact yet refined design&r."
				""
				"In this modpack, the maximum weapon level cap has been increased from the default &610&r to &630&r, in order to slow down player progression."
				""
				"Weapon Master also provides a highly comprehensive configuration system, with well-crafted visuals. Its weapon attribute progression system meets a wide range of player needs, and the versatility of its weapons ensures they remain useful even in late-game power scaling. &2It is hoped that this introduction has sparked your interest in this mod&r！"
			]
			icon: "weaponmaster:workstation"
			id: "1E13C34A1DBB2224"
			rewards: [{
				id: "218893B2BCD2628A"
				item: "simplehats:hatbag_epic"
				type: "item"
			}]
			subtitle: "The limits of Weapon Master"
			tasks: [{
				id: "50517FD1B3BF2E2C"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "Weapon Master！"
			x: 1.0d
			y: 5.0d
		}
